From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:51:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] EventStream: pass a failed poll to the stream instead of
 retrying it

Repository: crates.io crossterm 0.28.1 (archive SHA-256 829d955a...dea9c6)
Author: tomaszstaniak
Date: 2026-10-19
Platform scope: all targets (stream.rs is shared); found on AROS.
Upstream status: candidate (not submitted).
Problem: EventStream's helper thread calls poll_internal(None) in a loop and
ignores errors. When the terminal's input has ended, every poll fails at
once: the thread spins at full CPU and the stream is never woken, so the
program never learns that its terminal is gone. On AROS, closing a Limpet
window while Helix ran left the window on "Closing: waiting for process"
with QEMU at 99 % of a host core.
Change: an error ends the thread's wait like an event does; poll_next then
reads the error from the source and yields it.
Verification: on AROS One 1.3 with Limpet 0.6.1, closing the window while
hx runs now ends hx (Helix patch "End when the terminal's input closes").
---
 src/event/stream.rs | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/event/stream.rs b/src/event/stream.rs
index f27eb374b51479b222e7704b52c491fb79b28e75..fdd80d30787298f527c384f59d6932b6e7b85b2f 100644
--- a/src/event/stream.rs
+++ b/src/event/stream.rs
@@ -44,7 +44,11 @@ impl Default for EventStream {
         thread::spawn(move || {
             while let Ok(task) = receiver.recv() {
                 loop {
-                    if let Ok(true) = poll_internal(None, &EventFilter) {
+                    // An error (the terminal's input has ended) goes to the
+                    // stream as well: poll_next reads it from the source.
+                    // Ignoring it here retried the failed read for good, at
+                    // full CPU, and the stream never learned of it.
+                    if !matches!(poll_internal(None, &EventFilter), Ok(false)) {
                         break;
                     }
 
